  "id": "summation-effect",
  "term": "summation effect",
  "definition": "A summation effect is an increase in the overall sensory response when similar inputs are combined. In this study, stimulating more fingers at the same vibration frequency produced a larger brain response, showing that somatosensory signals can add together rather than being processed completely separately.",
